  "id": "COMPOUND:41429 - PROTEIN:5003",
  "verbalization": "Anandamide, a bioactive lipid, is implicated in multiple pathways that ultimately lead to the activation of ME-180. The evidence suggests that Anandamide acts as a target in several distinct molecular networks, with different compounds acting as intermediaries in these pathways. One pathway involves the FaDu cell line, where Anandamide directly targets this cell, which in turn is targeted by 21-(5-Formyl-1H-Pyrrol-2-Yl)Henicosanenitrile, which itself targets ME-180. Another pathway links Anandamide to the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which is targeted by Broussoaurone A, also leading to ME-180. A third pathway connects Anandamide to (+)-3-Methylcyclohexanone, which targets ME-180. These findings collectively indicate that Anandamide exerts its effects through multiple molecular mechanisms, with different compounds serving as intermediaries in the activation of ME-180. The strength of the evidence is consistent across these pathways, suggesting a broad involvement of Anandamide in the regulation of ME-180 through diverse biochemical interactions.",
